# The orbit means and ranges of the rows

The table of the `135` rows `(c, o)` with the denominators `p_d` and the scan results
`(T₁, M₁, m₁)` and `(T₃, M₃, m₃)` of the orbit sequences of `s = 1` and `s = 3`; the
orbit sequences of `s = 7` and `s = 5` are their rotations. The orbit mean of the row is
`T / (2^{14} · 10^8 p_d)` and the orbit range `(M - m) / (2^{14} · 10^8 p_d)`.

## Main definitions

* `CollatzPosDens.C3H17Values.rowTab`: the table.
* `CollatzPosDens.C3H17Values.meanVal`, `CollatzPosDens.C3H17Values.rangeVal`: the orbit mean and
  range read from the table.
* `CollatzPosDens.C3H17Values.RowMR`: the orbit means and ranges of a row are the table values.
-/

